AWPTCM-T30403 (1.0)  Check traffic is forwarded with static mroutes (IPv4)
Run date : 2026-09-10      Bench : tb470 (IE520)
Software : IE520-awplus_main-20260905-1714.rel  (AlliedWare Plus, build 09/04/26; bootloader pauld)
Result   : PASS
================================================================================

RESULT
  An IPv4 static mroute (ip mroute) provides the RPF for a multicast source that has
  no unicast route.  With the static mroute the multicast is forwarded; when it is
  removed the RPF fails and forwarding stops - cleanly, with no errors.
      WITH  ip mroute : show ip rpf -> RPF type STATIC ; receiver got 19/20 ;
                        (S,G) mroute iif=vlan40 -> oif=vlan82
      WITHOUT         : show ip rpf -> "failed, no route exists" ; receiver 0/20 ;
                        (S,G) mroute gone ; no error on removal            => PASS.
  Interfaces exercised as upstream/downstream: VLAN interfaces (iif vlan40 = upstream,
  oif vlan82 = downstream).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / multicast router : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0  (PIM-SM, SSM)
      static mroute      : ip mroute 10.10.50.0/24 10.10.40.2   (RPF via u5 on vlan40)
      NOTE: the unicast route to 10.10.50.0/27 was REMOVED first, so the static
            mroute is the ONLY RPF path to the source subnet - it is load-bearing.
  RPF neighbour          : u5  10.10.40.2 on vlan40 (a real PIM neighbour, so the
                           (S,G) upstream is valid)
  Host (one NIC, tagged sub-ifs on u4 port1.0.2):
      source injector : eth2.40 (vlan40) - sends from 10.10.50.5 (the remote source)
      receiver        : eth2.82 (vlan82) 10.10.82.20 - IGMPv3 SSM (S,G) join
  Group : 239.100.40.10  (in the SSM range 239.100.0.0/16)
  Source: 10.10.50.5  (reachable at u4 only via the static mroute)

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA.  The "remote" source 10.10.50.5 has no unicast route on the DUT; its RPF
  is supplied solely by the static mroute (verified with show ip rpf, type STATIC).
  The source is injected on the RPF/upstream interface (vlan40) with scapy; the
  receiver joins the (S,G) and is sniffed.  The static mroute is then removed and the
  same source is replayed.  Forwarding tracks the presence of the static mroute.
  Functional test.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG APPLIED   (running-config only, NOT saved to startup)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4
  ip multicast-routing ; service pim
  no ip route 10.10.50.0/27 10.10.40.2          <-- remove unicast route first
  ip mroute 10.10.50.0/24 10.10.40.2            <-- static mroute = the only RPF
  access-list 40 permit 239.100.0.0 0.0.255.255 ; ip pim ssm range 40
  interface vlan40  ip address 10.10.40.1/30 ; ip pim sparse-mode     (upstream/iif)
  interface vlan82  ip address 10.10.82.1/27 ; ip igmp ; ip pim sparse-mode (downstream/oif)
  interface port1.0.2  switchport trunk allowed vlan add 40,82

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 - WITH the static mroute: RPF resolves (static) and traffic forwards
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4# show ip rpf 10.10.50.5
  RPF interface: vlan40
  RPF neighbor: 10.10.40.2
  RPF route: 10.10.50.0/24
  RPF type: static                        <-- RPF supplied by the static mroute

### receiver joins IGMPv3 (10.10.50.5, 239.100.40.10); source injects 20 x UDP ###
WITH-MROUTE: source 10.10.50.5 (on vlan40) -> receiver got: 19 of 20

u4# show ip mroute 239.100.40.10
(10.10.50.5, 239.100.40.10), uptime 00:00:11, stat expires 00:03:19
Owner PIM-SM, Flags: TF
  Incoming interface: vlan40                    <-- upstream (matches the static RPF)
  Outgoing interface list:
    vlan82 (1)                                  <-- downstream
  => the static mroute lets the DUT RPF-accept the source on vlan40 and forward to
     the receiver on vlan82.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 - REMOVE the static mroute: RPF fails, forwarding stops, no error
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4(config)# no ip mroute 10.10.50.0/24        <-- accepted cleanly, no error emitted
u4# show ip rpf 10.10.50.5
RPF information for 10.10.50.5 failed, no route exists     <-- RPF is now gone

### same source replayed ###
NO-MROUTE: source 10.10.50.5 (on vlan40) -> receiver got: 0 of 20

u4# show ip mroute 239.100.40.10
  (no entry)                                    <-- the (S,G) is gone; nothing forwards
  => removing the static mroute removes the only RPF path to the source, the (S,G)
     tears down, and traffic stops.  Removal produced no errors.  PASS.
